====================================================================================================
Q. EXPLICIT ROBUSTNESS FLAGS
====================================================================================================
1. ROBUST to denominator: Wetlands & Coastal exceed Croplands in gardening SHARE under the invaded-plot
   denominator (OR 5.55 and 5.06) and under the AgriForest-dropped denominator (5.70, 5.23).
2. NOT ROBUST to denominator: the pooled 'Seminatural-pooled' class reverses sign. Under the invaded-plot
   denominator it looks gardening-rich (share 0.55, OR 5.34 vs Croplands); under the all-plots denominator
   (any gardening plot, 632 plots) it is the LOWEST class (OR 0.15, p<0.001). Reason: 17 invaded plots out
   of 347 -> 4.9 gardening occurrences per 100 plots vs 69.2 in Urban. Its 'style' is an artifact of tiny
   occurrence counts and is NOT an ecological signal; do not use it to argue that remote seminatural
   habitats are gardening hotspots.
3. Coniferous forests (0.88, n=8 occurrences) and Broad-leaved forests (1.00, n=4) shares are uninformative
   in isolation (separation in the 10-level model: infinite estimates, SE ~1e4); they contribute only via
   the pooled class.
4. Riparian's gardening share (0.365) is statistically indistinguishable from the overall mean
   (MC per-cell p=0.83) but it is the single AgriForest hotspot: 13 of 23 AgriForest occurrences,
   standardised residual +3.93, MC p=0.0006 -> the third pathway is not evenly spread either.
5. Context effects are partly collinear with habitat labels: context alone explains 4.5% of deviance,
   habitat labels 13.7%; habitat still adds beyond context (quasi-F=7.01, p=5e-06) while context adds only
   marginally beyond habitat (quasi-F=1.67, p=0.12; beta-binomial 2*dlogL=9.54 on 3 df, p=0.023).
   The WetCoastal contrast does NOT attenuate when urban/cropland cover, elevation and rainfall are added
   (1.28 -> 1.38 logit), so the wet/coastal gardening excess is not explained by those covariates.
6. Species non-independence is not modelled: 481 occurrences come from 77 unique species (no crosswalk to
   plots), so habitat contrasts carry residual species-level pseudoreplication; overdispersion was
   phi=0.98-1.10 and beta-binomial rho=0.018, i.e. little extra-binomial variance at plot level, which
   limits but does not eliminate this concern.

